<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hymettus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑμηττός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain near Athens</i>, <i>famed for its honey and its marble</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7,
				11, § 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin.
				2, 34, 112</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2, 6, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				702</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 88</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 1,
				396</span></i> et saep.— In <i>fem.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attica (perh. of the region about Hymettus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hymettĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>from
				Hymettus</i>, <i>Hymettian</i>: mel, Cic. Fragm.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 240, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				2, 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 284</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 3, 3, § 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trabes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 18, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
